"Let $p$ represent the profit on a single game, in dollars. Using the given probabilities, let's summarize this in a table.  If $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =0\\cdot f(0)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{3}{10})+5(\\frac{1}{5})+10(\\frac{3}{20}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{10}+1+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{10}{10}+\\frac{15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10} \\\\  & =3.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$\\,3.9.$" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360186 13194139535668 true] [17592186360185 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535668 true] [17592186360185 1041 "field-1" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360185 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360186 13194139535668 true] [17592186360185 1110 #uuid "8bbc6fe9-01bd-50c4-8516-b2272433b5a2" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360186 1034 "3.90" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360186 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535668 true] [17592186360186 1111 #uuid "25deffb2-a4f1-508b-a97f-33a409583e51" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360188 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1089 "q-5772" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1100 "What is the expected value of one roll of a ten-sided die?" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1113 #uuid "a1266b57-0f5e-5d57-8103-b87c9995abbf" 13194139535668 true] [17592186360187 1145 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n